run lint analysis over resolved scopes (check by default; --apply writes fixes)

Usage: dx lint|typecheck|format [--check] [--apply] [--here] [--affected] [scope ...] [-- bazel-options ...]

Arguments:
  [TARGETS]...
          Scopes to run on

  [BAZEL_OPTIONS]...
          Args after --

Options:
      --workspace <WORKSPACE>
          Use this workspace dir

  -q, --quiet[=<QUIET>]
          Hide summaries. =false turns off an inherited default
          
          [possible values: true, false]

  -v, --verbose[=<VERBOSE>]
          Show more logs. =false turns off an inherited default
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --color <COLOR>
          Set color output

      --build-slots <auto|n|off>
          Set build slots: auto, a count, or off

      --bazel-startup-option <TOKEN>
          Pass one Bazel startup option (repeatable)

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Set output format
          
          [possible values: text, diff, json]

      --include-edits
          Include full edits in JSON change records (needs --output json)

      --check
          Check without changing files

      --apply
          Write fixes to source files

      --fail-on <FAIL_ON>
          Fail on this severity

      --report <REPORT>
          Write a report file

      --here
          Use the current dir tree

      --affected
          Select targets affected by git changes

  -h, --help
          Print help

Scopes: explicit Bazel labels/patterns (//..., //pkg:target), or workspace-relative files/dirs resolved via Bazel query. Graph-scope commands select //... when no scope is supplied. Pass --here for the current directory tree instead (//path/...; //... at the root); --here cannot be combined with explicit scopes and never changes the no-flag default. --affected selects targets changed since the default branch merge-base plus their reverse dependencies; it cannot be combined with scopes or --here.
Exit codes: 0 success; 2 usage/scope/owner errors; 1 findings, operational failures, and Bazel failures (Bazel's code is not kept).
Output: --output text|diff|json; --report sarif=<destination> (repeatable).
Environment: NO_COLOR=<any> disables color; BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY=<dir> sets the workspace start. `dx --help` lists every DX_ default.

